WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.190
The second match of the Monaco Cup finals has begun.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.730
The topic is to make a sweetened bread
while on an uninhabited island.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.320
However...

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.900
Actually, I have a request.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.400
What?!

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.530
He wants us to set fire to the forest
after we’ve gotten the fruit?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.660
What can the chairman be thinking of?

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.250
Thus, the Japanese representatives found
themselves in a predicament, and that was...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.510
Because we’re surrounded by a sea of fire!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.130
What was that?!

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.390
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.350
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.600
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:46.190
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.790
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.560
And now, you must swim!

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.650
<i>Tai</i>-yaki-kun of the Southern Island!

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:29.120
How can this be?!

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:32.130
W-Why are we surrounded by a sea of fire?

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.460
I don’t know.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.130
But, the one thing I do know...

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.670
is that we’re going to die, without doubt.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.670
That’s giving up hope a little too soon, isn’t it?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.130
You’re usually so full of yourself, so why are you giving up so easily?

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.140
Why am I giving up so easily, you ask?!

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.010
Because there’s a spinning pyramid coming right at us!

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.140
What was that?!

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.900
Dodge it, Kawachi!

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.080
Sorry for the wait,
Japanese representatives.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.320
Are you all right?

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.910
What are you?!

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.590
Are <i>you</i> all right?

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.500
Now that I’m here,
you can rest at ease.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.590
Come, let’s run away together.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:22.600
Huh?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.600
A pathway has opened up from
the impact of that pyramid flying in!

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.420
Let’s run!

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.090
Hey!
Let’s run!

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.600
You’re just going to abandon me?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.670
How inhuman!

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.380
You’re the one that’s not human here!

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.760
It’s common sense to abandon a pyramid
that comes flying into a situation like this!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.610
Kawachi! Suwabara!

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.060
That pyramid’s a good guy.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:41.110
Please help him.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.370
Azuma!

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.080
You’re alive!

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.120
I was worried for a moment there.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.990
Truly a case in which the
mummy hunter becomes a mummy.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:51.950
Oh, shut up.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.000
Sorry.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.120
But Azuma, you’re alive.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.670
I’m so glad.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.420
You’re the man who defeated me.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.640
I had faith that you wouldn’t die that easily.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.640
By the way...

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.800
You’re the Egyptian representatives, right?

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.640
Why did you go through the
trouble of coming to help us?

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.900
Actually, we are not the Egyptian representatives.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:17.650
We are...

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:38.670
The Monaco Secret Police!

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.550
Monaco Secret Police
The Monaco Secret Police!

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.130
Monaco Secret Police

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.260
Let me explain.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:53.180
The Monaco Secret Police was established
to watch for any injustice in the Monaco Cup.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:56.020
It is a special unit directly under the King of Monaco.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.030
Muhammad, that’s the wrong ID.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:06.950
What’s this?!

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.950
What do you mean by “Secret Police”?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.320
While the Monaco Cup may be
a world tournament for bread,

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.330
about 1 trillion yen worth of money
is being passed around in the casino.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.960
Therefore, it is obvious for those who intend to undermine the integrity of the cup to appear.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:27.980
We believe that the head of the Management Committee, Yulrich Rame, is one of them.

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:33.310
We also believe that the fire in the forest
was most likely started under his orders.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:39.100
Well, without doubt, it’s that
three-tiered totem pole who’s responsible.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:44.200
Yes, it’s obvious that they took the fruit
for themselves and then started the fire.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.200
Perhaps, but we have no proof.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.360
Either way, in this manner, I have
been disguising myself as a pyramid.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:58.210
I will continue my behind-the-scenes
secret investigation to expose any injustice.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:02.000
You should all work hard so as to
not lose to any of their schemes.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.460
Yep!

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.290
I do remember there being a
pyramid on the plane, but...

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:11.050
nobody paid much attention to it,
thinking that it was some kind of luggage.

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:14.220
I mean, nobody would think that
there was a person inside, right?

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.270
Well, we shall take our leave of you now.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:18.970
But...

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:22.930
there’s got to be some other way to
do a behind-the-scenes investigation.

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.890
Wait, triangular one.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.570
I have one more question.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.980
Although Monaco’s a separate country...

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:32.650
it’s somewhat like a part of France.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:38.460
So, aren’t you and the King of
Monaco hoping for France to win?

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.460
Of course we are.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:47.170
But only if we are able to have a fair and square match.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:54.210
We do not wish for France to win by hindering other countries for selfish desires, like Rame.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.180
So, rest assured and fight.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.300
Very well.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.940
I’ll believe you.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.240
We set fire to the forest.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.280
Now, it’s impossible for Japan to get any fruit.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:15.190
After all, the topic is sweetened bread.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:18.030
Without fruit, they can’t make anything.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:19.660
Far from it...

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:24.090
They may have gotten caught
in the fire, and burned to death!

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.920
I see.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.470
Well done...

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.040
is what I’d like to say.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.010
However, it probably wasn’t good enough.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:39.930
I believe that the island has a variety of
potato similar to sweet potato, called umara.
Note: Umara is a Tahitian sweet potato.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.480
Even if you burn the forest,

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.440
you cannot get rid of a potato that grows in the earth.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.940
If they use this potato, they might be able to...

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.900
Just as expected of you, Monsieur Kirisaki.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.440
You are a cautious man.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.980
But, rest assured.

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:57.860
Unlike the Japanese sweet potato,

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.950
this variety of potato barely has any sweetness.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:04.710
Unless you add sugar, it’s barely edible.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.210
I wonder...

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:12.430
Rame, I pray that your lack of
foresight doesn’t lead to your destruction.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:30.280
It’s been raining for a while.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.080
Yeah.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.710
We sure picked up a big shell there.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.080
Yeah.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:40.080
Well, for now, we’ve collected enough water,

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.840
and the fire’s gone.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.250
We should call this rain a blessing, I guess...

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.550
But, all the fruit is gone.

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:49.590
The rain came too late.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.460
It might be impossible to make our bread now...

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.100
Oh, this is...

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.610
They’re potatoes.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.350
Potatoes?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.990
Good work, Azuma!

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.200
Potatoes have a tiny bit of sweetness in them!

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.570
We might be able to use them.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.160
What’s this?

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.370
Far from sweet,
they’re completely tasteless.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:19.070
What were you hoping for?

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.620
These aren’t Japanese potatoes.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:25.130
They haven’t undergone selective
breeding for easy human consumption.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.080
It’s natural for them to be tasteless.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.540
Disappointment.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.410
Hey, Suwabara, please light a fire.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:32.800
Sure, but what do you intend to do?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.550
Boil potatoes.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.300
Once they’re done, peel them.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:44.430
Then, if we crush ’em like this and strain ’em...

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.550
we can make potato-an.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.810
Note: Anko (<b>餡子) is sweet red bean paste; potato-an is sweet potato paste.
Potato-an? Like anko?</b>

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:50.520
Wait a bit.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.360
I just ate some, and these
potatoes are completely tasteless.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.820
If they’re not sweet, we can’t make a sweetened bread.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:58.530
You don’t need to worry.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.200
This way.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.040
See that?

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:05.290
What’s that?

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:07.290
A coconut tree?

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.170
Most of the forest burned down,
and we can’t use anything else, but...

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:15.000
the coconut trees were closer
to the beach, and were all right.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.130
I see!

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.790
Coconuts have milk!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:21.170
If we’re able to boil and concentrate it,
we might be able to get a sweet...

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:23.310
No, I don’t think it’ll work out so well.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:27.970
Natural coconut milk contains very little sugar.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.930
I don’t know how many coconuts
you plan on using for your concentrate,

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:33.820
but if you want to make it into
a sweet paste, you’ll need a lot.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:38.560
Also, there is a lot of material
in the coconut aside from sugar.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.360
If you cannot extract that,

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.740
after boiling it down, you’ll be
left with a strange flavor and smell.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.150
You may be right.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:48.660
Come to think of it, the milk
is only mildly sweet, so it’s bad.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.450
We don’t have a method to just
extract the sugar in it, anyway.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.750
What are you guys talking about?

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.620
I’m not going to use the nut itself.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:56.260
What was that?!

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:57.260
What?

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.590
I’m going to use the tree’s juice.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:01.670
In other words...

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.480
I’ll be using the palm sap!

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:04.720
Sap?!

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:17.310
Finally it’s the last day.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.070
Yep.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.070
The teams that have made bread so far are...

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:29.080
us, America, Vietnam and
China, leaving four countries behind.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.330
So, can we really call our scheme of
burning down the forest a success?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.840
If we hadn’t been distracted by the paradise we
were in, and had set the fire off a little earlier...

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:41.230
Our country might have been the
only one to succeed in making a bread.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.220
Perhaps.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:46.350
But, if we were to have been too
greedy, we might have been suspected.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.270
Well, those bothersome Japanese
representatives have disappeared,

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.560
and it would be sad if we had no matches at all.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.360
So, we should call it a success.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.610
Very true.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.070
The Kaysers seem very happy for some reason.

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:03.570
At any rate, I wonder if they’re all okay...

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:12.830
The rules state that the four countries to make the most delicious bread in a week will win.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.590
But, now that the
all-important fruit has been burned away,

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.100
it’s impossible to make a sweetened bread at all.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.340
Even if it’s Kazuma and the gang, we’re now done for.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:25.720
It’s a flare!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.720
That color’s the Japanese representatives.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.480
Send out the retrieval team immediately.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:31.100
Yes, Sir!

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.780
Welcome back, Japanese representatives.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:45.490
I knew it. That you’d come back.

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:46.950
Impossible!

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.330
We burned down the forest!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.830
So, how in the world did they...?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.000
Don’t panic, Edward.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.040
Most likely it’s because their time’s almost up.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.250
They figured that it’s better to have an
unsweetened bread than no bread at all.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.970
We have no reason to fear.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:00.960
Y-You’re right.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.650
You guys!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.190
I was waiting, Japanese representatives.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:24.950
At any rate, unlike all the other
countries who’ve made their bread so far...

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.530
you guys are pretty beat up, aren’t you?

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:29.700
That’s because, thanks to a
certain country hindering us,

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.910
we had to live on a deserted island for a week.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.420
Yeah, so excuse us for our filthy appearance.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.670
So, how about the bread...?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.560
Oh.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:47.180
Here you go!

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.520
What an ugly bread.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.310
Doesn’t look tasty at all.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.180
It kinda resembles <i>that</i>, doesn’t it?

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:58.100
While this may not look the best,

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:04.820
it’s the very sweet <i>Japan</i> #9 made
from palm sap and sweet potato paste.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:06.950
It’s Taiyaki-<i>Japan</i>!
Note: Taiyaki (<b>鯛焼き) is a fish-shaped pancake filled with bean jam.</b>

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.620
<i>Japan</i> #9.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.000
It’s Taiyaki-<i>Japan</i>!

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.170
P-Palm sap?!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.760
Don’t tell me that he really made a sweetened bread?!

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:23.750
Impossible!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.060
It can’t be!

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:28.050
I see.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.570
To make taiyaki from palm sap...

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:36.020
This year’s Japanese representatives really do come up with out-of-the-world ideas.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:44.820
There’s no filling in this taiyaki!

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:46.200
What was that?!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.580
To think that you tried to fool me!

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:50.450
How very lacking in common sense!

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.170
Well, of course.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:55.260
There’s no filling at the very tip of the tail.

00:14:59.050 --> 00:15:00.430
Oh, how silly of me.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.350
But, I like to have plenty of filling all
the way to the tip of the tail, you know...

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:04.640
Like we care!

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.350
Our stamina’s at the end of its tether
after a week of living on a deserted island.

00:15:08.350 --> 00:15:09.520
You’re going to make our hearts give out!

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:11.270
Oh. I’m so sorry.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:15.190
But, it’s a clown’s job to surprise people.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:16.940
It’s like an occupational disease.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.980
Always ready with a convenient excuse...

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:23.530
That happened after the
performance in Las Vegas was over.

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.450
Now, don’t be surprised, Bolneze.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.250
Believe it or not, we’ve received a
letter from the French President!

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.250
Really?!

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:30.160
Yeah.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:34.880
It seems that even the President has
heard about Quedam’s worldwide success.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:35.250
Huh?!

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:39.250
He wishes for us to have performance at home, in an opera house in Paris.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.460
Amazing!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.760
We’ve done it!

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:44.640
This is what they call going home in triumph!

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.500
It’s all thanks to you, Bolneze!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:50.140
All right! With this, even
my mom’s going to accept me.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.190
I’m going to call Ma!

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:51.940
I wonder if my grandfather will come to watch...
I’m going to call Ma!

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.900
I wonder if my grandfather will come to watch...

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.160
Everyone seems really happy.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:15:59.930
I’m glad.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.790
Since I don’t have any
relatives, I can’t understand, but...

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:08.950
I wonder what it feels like to be able to
boast to your country and your family...

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:10.450
Bolneze.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:14.170
This performance will also be a special one for you, right?

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.460
Yeah, I guess.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:17.950
It’s the performance in our home
country that we’ve always dreamed of.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.840
What are you saying?!

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:23.210
If this goes well, we may be able to find your parents!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:24.920
Oh, I see!

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.100
If it’s going to be a huge performance at home,

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:30.520
it’ll be all over the newspapers and television.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:34.930
If so many people know
about it, even my parents might...

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:36.810
Listen, Bolneze.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:40.930
Both for Quedam and for your own sake,
we must make this performance a success!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:41.930
Yes, Sir!

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:44.950
It’s a little embarrassing to say this,

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.940
but there was something
savage about my training after that.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.160
I piled practice upon more practice.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.000
My cloning technique, which
initially consisted of only 50 clones,

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:56.450
was increased to 150, which is
three times the original amount!

00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:58.430
I’m happy for you.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:16:59.460
However...

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:02.840
your prologue is really long, every single time.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:06.180
We’d really appreciate it if you
could hurry if up just this once.

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:09.760
If it was me, I’d just show a quick reaction, and...

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.100
I-I can’t...

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:12.770
I feel weird.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.970
My head’s kinda spinning, and...

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:18.940
But, then...

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:19.720
Just listen to us, will you?!

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:22.690
Bolneze!

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:23.720
What happened?!

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:24.980
What happened?!

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:26.700
What’s wrong?

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.160
Bolneze!

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.230
Hey, what’s wrong?

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:31.250
Call an ambulance!

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:38.130
Because I practiced too hard, I pulled several muscles.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.350
This is terrible.

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:47.020
To heal, it’s going to take at least...

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.550
Yeah... Probably about three months.

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:50.960
Huh?!

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:52.390
No way!

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:53.930
The performance is next month!

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:55.100
We must somehow...

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.930
Calm down, Bolneze.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:17:59.520
Please.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.820
Isn’t there some...

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.780
Isn’t there some way of curing me by then?

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:04.480
Doctor!

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:08.000
To tell you the truth, with the medical
technology that’s currently available...

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:12.940
Well, I’ve never even heard of a patient
who... pulled all the muscles in his body.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:14.790
I’m stupid.

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:16.500
I’m so stupid!

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.130
My one chance, and...

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:23.660
I can’t face them.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.170
Bolneze.

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:31.180
Cheer up, Bolneze!

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:33.350
You don’t have to worry about us.

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:34.350
Yeah!

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.640
We’ve gotten this far thanks to you!

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:37.770
Exactly.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:40.600
Besides, it’s not like this is the
only time we can perform at home.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:42.190
I’m sure we’ll have another chance someday.

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:44.030
Yeah. We’ll have another chance.

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:46.020
Thank you, everyone.

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:48.560
Hey!

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.820
Where do you think you’re taking Bolneze?!

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:51.810
Who are you?!

00:18:54.790 --> 00:18:55.840
Me?

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.870
I’m Kid.

00:18:57.870 --> 00:18:58.790
A masseur.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.580
A masseur?!

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.340
Yeah.

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:04.280
I’ve been told that my touch can
make fountains of life bubble forth...

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:06.290
by Marilyn Monroe.

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:09.340
By Marilyn Monroe?!

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:11.560
Wasn’t that Namikoshi Tokujiro?

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:11.660
Note: Namikoshi Tokujiro was a famous shiatsu specialist who was known to have treated Marilyn Monroe.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.680
I was confused for a while.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.460
I mean, that guy had come
out of nowhere, and seemed fake.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:20.470
But, the moment that he touched my shoulder...

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:25.180
I could raise my immobile arm!

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.110
I’m Kid.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:28.360
I’m a fan of yours.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:30.180
I’d like to help you.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:33.740
I still wasn’t sure whether I could trust him,

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:36.580
but I couldn’t deny the miracles
occurring before my very eyes.

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:39.960
So, I entrusted both my body and soul to him.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:42.920
Oh, this massage is amazing.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.210
I didn’t know that France had
such a wonderful massage technique...

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.340
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:50.840
This is not a French-shiki massage.
Note: Shiki (<b>式) means “style.”</b>

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:52.470
This is Thai-shiki.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:53.710
Thai-shiki?!

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:55.270
Thai-shiki.

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:56.520
<i>Tai</i>-shiki.

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:57.650
<i>Tai</i>-yaki.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:19:59.730
Taiyaki.

00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.990
Taiyaki!

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:04.900
The amazing Thai-shiki!

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:07.780
I mean, taiyaki, Japanese representatives!

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:09.720
You have passed, without a doubt.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:11.150
What was that?!

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.240
Th-Then...

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:15.950
Of course, since the rules
state that the best four teams win...

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:20.080
I guess we have no choice
but to fail some other country.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:23.250
I’ll make the official announcement
after the other countries have returned.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:24.460
N-No way!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:26.420
Calm down, Edward!

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.170
We’re the top seeded French representatives!

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:31.050
There’s no way we’d fail.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:32.260
Turn, turn, turn, turn.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:34.460
Well, leaving that aside...

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:37.260
Actually, Japanese representatives,

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:41.600
though the performance in Paris was a great success...

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.940
In the end, my parents never did turn up.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:47.730
However...

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:51.940
thanks to this taiyaki-pan, I once again have hope.

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:56.670
You were able to make this wonderful bread

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:59.580
under the desperate conditions at the deserted island.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.900
So, someday, I’m sure that I’ll find my parents!

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.460
So...

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:09.410
Th-This is...

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.690
Extreme sunstroke!

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:13.220
Oh, you poor things...

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:16.290
Well, you were on a deserted island for a whole week.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.350
So, your stamina is at a low.

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:21.890
Also, while it may be evening, you’re
on the deck of a boat in a tropical sea,

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.680
so it’s still a burning hell.

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:26.180
That’s not where the problem lies.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.430
Your stories are just too long.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:29.760
Stop!

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:32.520
You will hurt yourselves if you talk any more than that!

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.070
I shall take you to the clinic right away.

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:36.620
The officials should go collect the representatives

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:39.330
from Korea, Egypt and Denmark, who are still on the island.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.020
We will sail immediately!

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:46.790
I’m sure that there should be proof

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:50.680
linking the French representatives and
Rame to the sabotage somewhere here.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:52.510
That is...

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:54.550
A communicator!

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:58.050
That’s probably the kind that uses satellite signals!

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:02.060
I’m sure that the French representatives must have used it to contact Rame.

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:04.850
If we can study this communicator...

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:06.600
Cleo! Muhammad!

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:08.050
I’ve found the proof!

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:14.630
This time, unfortunately, we
were not able to find any proof.

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:16.980
Yeah, we’ve reached the time limit.

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:18.990
By the way, where’s Pharaoh-sama?

00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:22.830
The officials from the boat
forced everyone to come along, so...

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:24.790
he must be on board.

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:26.990
Yeah, probably in the luggage hold.

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:28.620
Cleo!

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:31.090
Muhammad!

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:08.130
Dang, does this ever feel good!

00:24:08.130 --> 00:24:10.370
Farewell, Japanese Representatives.

00:24:10.370 --> 00:24:14.600
That dive is a one-way ticket of no return.

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:16.430
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:18.710
A Dive into Hell!! A New Scheme!

00:24:18.710 --> 00:24:19.980
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:22.990 --> 00:24:26.180
Thai-style massage is incredible! And also known as Nuad Boran!

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:28.700
Its origins go back 2500 hundred years, you know.

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:31.710
The combination of finger massage and stretching relieves stress and improves health!

00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:33.670
Ehhh?!?
